# Everything Next writes into this app. `next build` creates the tsconfig.json
# and the next-env.d.ts as well as .next, because it verifies a TypeScript
# toolchain even with `typescript.ignoreBuildErrors`
# (`apps/asas-next/node_modules/next/dist/lib/verify-typescript-setup.js` `writeConfigurationDefaults)(` and `writeAppTypeDeclarations`).
# None of the three is committed: the repository's single root tsconfig.json is
# what typechecks this app, and #42 is explicit that it is not split.
#
# How the generated tsconfig.json compares to the root one: `next.config.ts`,
# beside the `typescript` key.
.next/
next-env.d.ts
tsconfig.json
